# service_gap_mapper_unknown_twice: A mapper-ref buffer (type 15) over mapping ID 99, which nothing mapped, used by three execs, then one over mapped surface 1. The mapper has no surface for 99, so every exec using it faults ("Attempting to create mapper ref against invalid surface", resources_mapper_buffer). In the service each attempt asks the host again (the service caches only surfaces it got), and from the second on the host already holds an entry for 99 ("Failed to emplace surface"); the outcome is the same. The buffer over surface 1 still works. Map and isolate setups only: the IOSurface host device needs a memory map.
